      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay, i get that the major organizations say that. but some people argue that if you look at the actual biological evidence of chromosomes and hormones, the distinction between sex and gender is basically just a social layer and doesn't change the underlying biological reality. isn't it possible that the \"consensus\" is just following a specific social framework rather than being purely based on biological facts?",
